#   * <module> The attractor library: the one catalogue of the published functions
#
# A proposal of 2026-09-30, on the stack of grammar compression with
# noinline attractors, then recursive typing, then compilation. An
# ATTRACTOR is a non-inline function of the library, a closed beta eta
# normal form, recognised by its content address once a setting has
# compressed a program (beta, eta and their reverses): the criterion is the
# code's content address.
#
# ONE CATALOGUE, ONE ADDRESS. This module is the catalogue of APIs, the
# only one. Its address is the
# content address of the attractor's beta eta normal form, attractor_address/2.
# The reasons for this address over the code name of the closure a term
# reduces to under weak_head (`doc/contest_api_catalogue.pl`, api_address/2):
# - it depends on no evaluation strategy: two spellings of one function with
#   a normal form have one normal form (confluence), whatever reduction
#   reached it;
# - it is the address the call restoration library already uses
#   (prolog/gezi/call_restoration.pl);
# - a recursive function has no normal form as a whole, so its old address
#   named whichever closure weak_head happened to reach; here it is the
#   normal form of its body (below), which is fixed.
# `doc/contest_api_catalogue.pl` and its addresses are DEPRECATED.
# INCOMPATIBILITY: a layer that keys a replacement by api_address/2,
# merge_api_address/2 or inheritance_api_addresses/2 moves to
# attractor_address/2; the entries keep the old catalogue's names, so the
# move is a change of address only. The inheritance calculus entries
# (inheritance_api/5) are not carried over: their programs hold labels,
# which the judgment no longer has.
#
# THE ENTRIES, `attractor(Name, Kind, Function)`, in the order of
# definition, a later one written with earlier ones:
# - Kind is `constructor` for a Scott constructor, or
#   `function(Dependencies, Recursion)`, Dependencies the entries themselves;
# - Function is the de Bruijn term (`lambda/1`, `apply/2`, `variable/1`),
#   the beta eta normal form of the entry's source (attractor_source/2),
#   stored in corpora/contest_attractor_normal_forms.pl, which
#   doc/contest_attractor_normal_forms.pl generates with the normaliser
#   prolog/gezi/old_corpora/beta_eta_normalisation.pl.
# A function has a native implementation when attractor_reference/3 of
# prolog/gezi/old_corpora/attractor_references.pl has a clause for it.
#
# THE API DECLARATIONS ONLY. This file holds the entries, their sources,
# their normal forms, their spellings, their addresses and the types of the
# native references' arguments and results.
# The native references and the normaliser are reference implementations in
# prolog/gezi/, which this file does not load.
#
# RECURSION. A recursive function has no normal form as a whole, so the
# library holds the normal form of its body, with its dependencies d1 ... dj,
# the functions of Dependencies, as leading parameters:
#
#     T = \d1 ... \dj. \self. \a1 ... \ak. B
#
# - `self_application`: the function is F = T D (T D), B calling it as
#   `self self`; the binary arithmetic of corpora/contest_merge_dynamic.pl is
#   written this way (multiplication's doubling, a beta redex there, is
#   contracted here);
# - `fixpoint`: the function is F = Y (T D), Y the prelude's fixpoint
#   combinator, B calling it as `self`; the prelude's recursive functions are
#   written this way (corpora/prelude_clauses.pl);
# - `none`: a function that does not recur, F = T D.
# Y has no normal form and is no attractor: it is how a `fixpoint` function
# is tied, function_surface/3.
#
# THE LIBRARY in the call restoration library's format is attractor_library/1: `Name-Function` in
# the order of definition.
#
# SPELLINGS. attractor_surface(Name, Spelling, Surface) builds a fresh
# surface term of Function. `direct` is Function itself. `respelled` has the
# same beta eta class, built by reverse beta steps only: every application
# whose head is a variable, x A1 ... An, is written ((\z. z) x) A1 ... An, so
# that no closure of the respelled term has the attractor's code and a
# forward beta step at each such head gives Function back.

#   attractor_entry(?Name, ?Kind), in the order of definition, each entry
#   bound by name (entry_<name>) before the table, so that a function's
#   dependencies are the entries themselves, not their names.
#
# The kind is a constructor of attractors/kind, constructor or function, a
# function's recursion a constructor of attractors/recursion, none,
# self_application or fixpoint. The name is a text for the host, which
# looks an attractor up by it (functionSurface; names pointing out of the
# mixin tree). Each other text is from_cbor of a string
# literal, a Scott list of bytes, imported from corpora/library/text/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
